"\n<div class=\"brand-bar\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"brand-logo\"><div class=\"brand-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div></div>\n<header class=\"lk-hd\"><div class=\"lk-topic\"><svg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"8.5\"></circle><path d=\"M8.5 12.2l2.5 2.3 4.5-5\"></path></svg></div><div class=\"lk-kicker\">Lektion</div><div class=\"lk-big\">12</div><h1>현재완료</h1><div class=\"lk-de\">Das Perfekt</div><div class=\"lk-intro\">독일어로 지난 일을 말할 때는 주로 현재완료를 써요.<br>보조 동사 haben이나 sein이 두 번째 자리에서 활용되고, 과거분사가 문장 끝에 와요 — Ich <strong>habe</strong> gestern Deutsch <strong>gelernt</strong>.<br>이 과에서는 과거분사를 만드는 모든 규칙과, haben과 sein을 고르는 기준을 정리해요.<div class=\"x-goals\"><div class=\"x-goals-t\">이 과에서 익힐 것</div><div class=\"x-goal\">보조 동사는 두 번째, 과거분사는 끝 — 현재완료의 문장 괄호를 만들어요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">규칙 동사 ge-…-t, 불규칙 동사 ge-…-en, 혼합 동사의 과거분사를 만들어요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">분리동사·비분리동사·-ieren 동사의 과거분사를 만들어요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">이동·상태 변화 동사와 sein·bleiben·werden·passieren에는 sein을 써요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">자주 쓰는 불규칙 과거분사를 외워요</div></div></div></header>\n<div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge review-badge\">복습</span><span class=\"sub-title\">10·11과 복습</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> '나는 7시에 일어나요.' (aufstehen)</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Ich stehe auf um 7 Uhr.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ich stehe um 7 Uhr aufstehen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Ich stehe um 7 Uhr auf.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Ich aufstehe um 7 Uhr.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">접두어 auf는 문장 끝 (11과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Ich ____ die Frage nicht. <span class=\"qh\">verstehen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) verstehen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) verstehst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) stehe … ver</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) verstehe</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ver-는 비분리 (11과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Du ____ hier nicht parken. <span class=\"qh\">여기 주차하면 안 돼</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) darfst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) sollst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) musst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) kannst</button></div><div class=\"qe\">금지 → nicht dürfen (10과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Ich ____ heute lange arbeiten. <span class=\"qh\">오늘 오래 일해야 해요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) müssen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) müsse</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) musst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) muss</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ich → muss, 어미 없음 (10과).</div></div></div>\n<section id=\"sec-A\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">A</span><h2>한국어로 먼저 보기</h2></div><p>한국어는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span> 하나에 '-았/었-'을 넣어서 과거를 말해요 — 배우다 → 배웠다, 가다 → 갔다.<br>독일어 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재완료<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재완료</span>말할 때 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. haben/sein + 과거분사로 만들어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.</span></span></span>는 동사 두 부분으로 과거를 말해요.<br>habe가 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">두 번째 자리<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">두 번째 자리</span>평서문에서 주어에 맞춰 바꾼 동사가 서는 자리예요. 독일어 어순의 가장 중요한 규칙이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich lerne Deutsch. · Heute lerne ich Deutsch.</span></span></span>에 오고, '배웠다'에 해당하는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거분사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거분사</span>완료형과 수동태를 만들 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 대부분 ge-로 시작해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: gelernt · gegangen · verstanden</span></span></span> gelernt가 문장 끝에 와요.</p><div class=\"dgm\"><div class=\"dgm-cap\">한국어는 동사 하나, 독일어는 두 부분</div><div class=\"klam\"><div class=\"klam-cells\"><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-pos\">주어</span><span class=\"klam-w\">나는</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-pos\">목적어</span><span class=\"klam-w\">독일어를</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-v\"><span class=\"klam-pos\">동사</span><span class=\"klam-w\">배웠다</span></div></div><div class=\"klam-tr\">한국어 — 동사 하나</div></div><div class=\"klam\"><div class=\"klam-cells\"><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">1</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">Ich</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-v\"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">2</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">habe</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">Deutsch</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-inf\"><span class=\"klam-pos\">끝</span><span class=\"klam-w\">gelernt</span></div></div><div class=\"klam-tr\">독일어 — 보조 동사 + 과거분사</div></div><div class=\"dgm-note\">이름은 '현재완료'이지만, 말할 때 쓰는 기본 과거예요. 대화·메시지·편지에서 지난 일을 거의 모두 현재완료로 말해요.</div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-B\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">B</span><h2>문장 괄호 — 보조 동사는 두 번째, 과거분사는 끝</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재완료<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재완료</span>말할 때 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. haben/sein + 과거분사로 만들어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.</span></span></span>는 haben이나 sein을 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">두 번째 자리<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">두 번째 자리</span>평서문에서 주어에 맞춰 바꾼 동사가 서는 자리예요. 독일어 어순의 가장 중요한 규칙이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich lerne Deutsch. · Heute lerne ich Deutsch.</span></span></span>에, <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거분사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거분사</span>완료형과 수동태를 만들 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 대부분 ge-로 시작해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: gelernt · gegangen · verstanden</span></span></span>를 맨 끝에 놓아요 — Ich <strong>habe</strong> Deutsch <strong>gelernt</strong>.</p></div></div><p><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">보조 동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">보조 동사</span>완료형·미래형·수동태를 만들 때 두 번째 자리에서 인칭과 시제만 맡는 haben·sein·werden이에요. 화법조동사와는 다른 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe gelernt. → habe</span></span></span> haben·sein만 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">주어<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">주어</span>문장에서 동작이나 상태의 주인이에요. 독일어 주어는 1격이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Der Hund schläft. → der Hund</span></span></span>에 맞춰 활용하고, 과거분사는 모양이 바뀌지 않아요.</p><div class=\"klam\"><div class=\"klam-cells\"><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">1</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">Wir</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-v\"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">2</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">haben</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">gestern</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">Fußball</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-inf\"><span class=\"klam-pos\">끝</span><span class=\"klam-w\">gespielt</span></div></div><div class=\"klam-tr\">우리는 어제 축구를 했어요.</div></div><div class=\"klam\"><div class=\"klam-cells\"><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">1</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">Gestern</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-v\"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">2</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">bin</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">ich</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">nach Hause</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-inf\"><span class=\"klam-pos\">끝</span><span class=\"klam-w\">gegangen</span></div></div><div class=\"klam-tr\">어제 나는 집에 갔어요.</div></div><div class=\"klam\"><div class=\"klam-cells\"><div class=\"klam-c klam-v\"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">1</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">Hast</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">du</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">den Film</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-inf\"><span class=\"klam-pos\">끝</span><span class=\"klam-w\">gesehen</span></div></div><div class=\"klam-tr\">그 영화 봤어?</div></div><div class=\"klam\"><div class=\"klam-cells\"><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">1</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">Wann</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-v\"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">2</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">ist</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">der Zug</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-inf\"><span class=\"klam-pos\">끝</span><span class=\"klam-w\">angekommen</span></div></div><div class=\"klam-tr\">기차가 언제 도착했어요?</div></div><div class=\"callout callout-key\"><span class=\"co-badge \">보조 동사는 화법조동사와 달라요</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">현재완료의 haben·sein은 '가지다·~⁠이다'라는 뜻이 없고, <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">인칭<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">인칭</span>말하는 나(1인칭), 듣는 너(2인칭), 그 밖의 사람·사물(3인칭)로 나누는 구분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich 1인칭 · du 2인칭 · er 3인칭</span></span></span>과 시제만 맡는 보조 동사예요. 뜻은 과거분사가 나타내요.<br>10과의 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">화법조동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">화법조동사</span>능력·허락·의무·의지 같은 뜻을 더해 주는 동사예요. 본동사는 원형으로 문장 끝에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: können · dürfen · müssen · sollen · wollen · mögen</span></span></span>(können·müssen…)와는 다른 무리예요.</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-C\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">C</span><h2>과거분사 만들기 — 기본 형태</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">규칙 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 ge- + <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어간<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어간</span>동사원형에서 끝의 -en(-n)을 뗀 부분이에요. 여기에 인칭어미를 붙여요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen → lern-</span></span></span> + -t예요 — lernen → <strong>ge</strong>lern<strong>t</strong>. 불규칙 동사는 ge- + … + -en이 많아요 — sehen → <strong>ge</strong>seh<strong>en</strong>.</p></div></div><h3>① 규칙 동사 — ge + 어간 + t</h3><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left\"><thead><tr><th>원형</th><th>과거분사</th><th>비고</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>lernen</td><td><strong>ge</strong>lern<strong>t</strong></td></tr><tr><td>machen · kaufen · spielen</td><td><strong>ge</strong>mach<strong>t</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>kauf<strong>t</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>spiel<strong>t</strong></td></tr><tr><td>wohnen · hören · sagen</td><td><strong>ge</strong>wohn<strong>t</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>hör<strong>t</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>sag<strong>t</strong></td></tr><tr><td>arbeiten · warten · kosten</td><td><strong>ge</strong>arbeit<strong>et</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>wart<strong>et</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>kost<strong>et</strong></td><td>어간 -t·-d → -et</td></tr><tr><td>öffnen · regnen</td><td><strong>ge</strong>öffn<strong>et</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>regn<strong>et</strong></td><td>-ffn·-gn → -et</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>② 불규칙 동사 — ge + 어간 + en, 모음이 바뀌기도 해요</h3><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left\"><thead><tr><th>원형</th><th>과거분사</th><th>모음</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>sehen · lesen · geben</td><td><strong>ge</strong>seh<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>les<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>geb<strong>en</strong></td><td>그대로</td></tr><tr><td>fahren · schlafen · kommen</td><td><strong>ge</strong>fahr<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>schlaf<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>komm<strong>en</strong></td><td>그대로</td></tr><tr><td>sprechen · helfen · nehmen</td><td><strong>ge</strong>spr<span class=\"x-e\">o</span>ch<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>h<span class=\"x-e\">o</span>lf<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>n<span class=\"x-e\">o</span>mm<strong>en</strong></td><td>e → o</td></tr><tr><td>trinken · finden · singen</td><td><strong>ge</strong>tr<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>nk<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>f<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>nd<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>s<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>ng<strong>en</strong></td><td>i → u</td></tr><tr><td>schreiben · bleiben</td><td><strong>ge</strong>schr<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>b<strong>en</strong> · <strong>ge</strong>bl<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>b<strong>en</strong></td><td>ei → ie</td></tr><tr><td>gehen · stehen · sitzen</td><td><strong>ge</strong>g<span class=\"x-e\">ang</span>en · <strong>ge</strong>st<span class=\"x-e\">and</span>en · <strong>ge</strong>s<span class=\"x-e\">ess</span>en</td><td>모양이 크게 바뀜</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>③ 혼합 동사 — ge + 바뀐 어간 + t</h3><p>불규칙처럼 모음이 바뀌지만 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어미<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어미</span>단어 끝에 붙어 문법 정보를 나타내는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lern-e · gut-er · Kind-er</span></span></span>는 규칙 동사처럼 -t예요.</p><div class=\"exl\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">bringen → <strong>ge</strong>br<span class=\"x-e\">ach</span><strong>t</strong></span><span class=\"exl-ko\">가져오다</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">denken → <strong>ge</strong>d<span class=\"x-e\">ach</span><strong>t</strong></span><span class=\"exl-ko\">생각하다</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">kennen → <strong>ge</strong>k<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nn<strong>t</strong></span><span class=\"exl-ko\">알다</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">wissen → <strong>ge</strong>w<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>ss<strong>t</strong></span><span class=\"exl-ko\">알다</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">nennen · rennen → <strong>ge</strong>nannt · <strong>ge</strong>rannt</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">부르다 · 달리다</span></div></div><h3>④ sein · haben · werden</h3><div class=\"exl\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">sein → <strong>gewesen</strong> · haben → <strong>gehabt</strong> · werden → <strong>geworden</strong></span></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">과거분사 만들기</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> machen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) gemacht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) gemachen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) gemachet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) machte</button></div><div class=\"qe\">규칙 → ge + mach + t.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> arbeiten의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) gearbeiten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) gearbeitet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) arbeitet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) gearbeitt</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -t → ge + arbeit + et.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> trinken의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) getrankt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) getrunken</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) getrinkt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) getrinken</button></div><div class=\"qe\">불규칙 i → u, -en.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> schreiben의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) geschrieben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) geschreiben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) geschriebt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) geschreibt</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ei → ie, -en.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> bringen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) gebringt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) gebrungen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) gebracht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) gebrachen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">혼합 동사 → ge + brach + t.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> gehen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) gegehen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) gangen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) gegangen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) gegeht</button></div><div class=\"qe\">불규칙 → gegangen.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">7.</strong> wissen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) gewussen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) gewusst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) gewissen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) gewisst</button></div><div class=\"qe\">혼합 동사 → gewusst.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-D\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">D</span><h2>ge-의 자리 — 분리동사 · 비분리동사 · -ieren 동사</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">분리동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">분리동사</span>앞부분(접두어)이 문장 끝으로 떨어져 나가는 동사예요. 접두어에 강세가 있어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: aufstehen → Ich stehe um 7 Uhr auf.</span></span></span>는 ge-가 가운데로 들어가요(auf<strong>ge</strong>standen). be-·ver- <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>와 -ieren 동사는 ge-가 붙지 않아요(verstanden · studiert).</p></div></div><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>동사 종류</th><th>규칙</th><th>예</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>분리동사</td><td>접두어 + <strong>ge</strong> + 어간</td><td>einkaufen → ein<strong>ge</strong>kauft · aufstehen → auf<strong>ge</strong>standen · anrufen → an<strong>ge</strong>rufen · fernsehen → fern<strong>ge</strong>sehen</td></tr><tr><td>비분리동사</td><td><strong>ge 없음</strong></td><td>besuchen → besucht · bezahlen → bezahlt · verstehen → verstanden · vergessen → vergessen · erzählen → erzählt · bekommen → bekommen</td></tr><tr><td>-ieren 동사</td><td><strong>ge 없음</strong>, -t</td><td>studieren → studiert · telefonieren → telefoniert · fotografieren → fotografiert · passieren → passiert</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-key\"><span class=\"co-badge \">강세가 첫 음절에 없으면 ge가 없어요</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">ge-는 강세 있는 첫 음절 앞에만 붙어요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">비분리동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">비분리동사</span>be-·ver- 같은 접두어가 동사에서 떨어지지 않는 동사예요. 접두어에 강세가 없어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: verstehen → Ich verstehe das.</span></span></span>(ver<strong>STEH</strong>en)와 -ieren 동사(stu<strong>DIER</strong>en)는 첫 음절에 강세가 없어서 ge가 붙지 않아요.</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">ge-의 자리</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> anrufen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) angerufet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) angerufen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) anrufen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) geanrufen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">분리동사 → 접두어 + ge + 어간.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> besuchen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) besucht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) begesucht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) gebesucht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) besuchen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">be-는 비분리 → ge 없음.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> studieren의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) gestudieren</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) studieren</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) gestudiert</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) studiert</button></div><div class=\"qe\">-ieren 동사 → ge 없음.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> einschlafen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) eingeschlaft</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) einschlafen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) eingeschlafen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) geeinschlafen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">분리 + 불규칙 → ein + ge + schlafen.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> vergessen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) vergegessen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) vergesst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) gevergessen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) vergessen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">비분리 + 불규칙 → 원형과 모양이 같아요.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-E\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">E</span><h2>haben이냐 sein이냐</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">대부분은 haben을 써요. 장소를 옮기는 동작(gehen·fahren)과 상태가 바뀌는 일(aufstehen·einschlafen)은 sein이에요.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-scroll\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 250\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"현재완료에서 sein을 쓰는 동사와 haben을 쓰는 동사\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><marker id=\"haben_sein-ink\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mki\"/></marker><marker id=\"haben_sein-acc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mka\"/></marker><marker id=\"haben_sein-ok\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mko\"/></marker><marker id=\"haben_sein-no\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mkn\"/></marker><marker id=\"haben_sein-w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mkw\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"10.0\" y=\"10.0\" width=\"285.0\" height=\"230.0\" rx=\"12\" class=\"f-boxo\"/><text x=\"152.0\" y=\"40.0\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-okt\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">sein</tspan> — 움직임 · 상태 변화</text><circle cx=\"36.0\" cy=\"84.0\" r=\"9.0\" class=\"f-fok\"/><circle cx=\"136.0\" cy=\"84.0\" r=\"9.0\" class=\"f-fok\"/><line x1=\"48.0\" y1=\"84.0\" x2=\"123.0\" y2=\"84.0\" class=\"f-lo\" marker-end=\"url(#haben_sein-ok)\"/><text x=\"36.0\" y=\"108.0\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-m\" font-weight=\"700\">A</text><text x=\"136.0\" y=\"108.0\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-m\" font-weight=\"700\">B</text><text x=\"166.0\" y=\"82.0\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-t\">gehen</text><text x=\"166.0\" y=\"101.0\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-m\">fahren · kommen</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"132.0\" width=\"62.0\" height=\"30.0\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"51.0\" y=\"152.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-m\">깨어 있음</text><rect x=\"104.0\" y=\"132.0\" width=\"46.0\" height=\"30.0\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"127.0\" y=\"152.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-m\">잠듦</text><line x1=\"84.0\" y1=\"147.0\" x2=\"101.0\" y2=\"147.0\" class=\"f-lo\" marker-end=\"url(#haben_sein-ok)\"/><text x=\"166.0\" y=\"145.0\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-t\">einschlafen</text><text x=\"166.0\" y=\"164.0\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-m\">aufstehen · werden</text><text x=\"152.0\" y=\"212.0\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\">Ich <tspan font-weight=\"700\">bin</tspan> eingeschlafen.</text><rect x=\"305.0\" y=\"10.0\" width=\"285.0\" height=\"230.0\" rx=\"12\" class=\"f-boxa\"/><text x=\"447.0\" y=\"40.0\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-a\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">haben</tspan> — 나머지 대부분</text><text x=\"447.0\" y=\"92.0\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\">Ich <tspan font-weight=\"700\">habe</tspan> gegessen.</text><text x=\"447.0\" y=\"126.0\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\">Ich <tspan font-weight=\"700\">habe</tspan> Deutsch gelernt.</text><text x=\"447.0\" y=\"160.0\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\">Ich <tspan font-weight=\"700\">habe</tspan> geschlafen.</text><text x=\"447.0\" y=\"212.0\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-m\">schlafen은 haben, einschlafen은 sein</text></svg></div><figcaption>장소 이동·상태 변화는 sein, 나머지는 haben</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" alt=\"Er ist auf dem Sofa eingeschlafen. 그는 소파에서 잠들었어요. 상태가 바뀌어서 sein이에요.\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><div><span class=\"ph-de\">Er <strong>ist</strong> auf dem Sofa <strong>eingeschlafen</strong>.</span><span class=\"ph-ko\">그는 소파에서 잠들었어요. 상태가 바뀌어서 sein이에요.</span></div></figcaption></figure><p>대부분의 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 haben과 함께 써요. 아래 동사들만 sein과 함께 써요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>무리</th><th>동사</th><th>예</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>① 장소 이동 (목적어 없이)</td><td>gehen · kommen · fahren · fliegen · laufen · reisen · steigen · fallen · ziehen(이사하다)</td><td>Ich <strong>bin</strong> nach Berlin <strong>gefahren</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>② 상태 변화</td><td>aufstehen · aufwachen · einschlafen · werden · sterben · wachsen</td><td>Er <strong>ist</strong> Lehrer <strong>geworden</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>③ 그 밖</td><td>sein · bleiben · passieren · begegnen</td><td>Wir <strong>sind</strong> zu Hause <strong>geblieben</strong>. · Was <strong>ist passiert</strong>?</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-key\"><span class=\"co-badge \">4격 목적어가 있으면 haben</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">fahren도 '~⁠을 운전하다'처럼 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">4격<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">4격</span>주로 '~을/를'을 나타내는 자리예요. 동작을 받는 대상이고, für·ohne 같은 전치사 뒤에도 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich sehe den Mann. 그 남자를 봐요.</span></span></span> <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">목적어<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">목적어</span>동사의 동작을 받는 말이에요. 독일어에서는 주로 4격이나 3격이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich sehe den Film. → den Film</span></span></span>가 있으면 haben이에요.<br>Ich <strong>bin</strong> nach Hamburg <strong>gefahren</strong>. 함부르크에 갔어요. · Ich <strong>habe</strong> das Auto in die Garage <strong>gefahren</strong>. 차를 차고에 넣었어요.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">schlafen은 haben, einschlafen은 sein</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">잠을 자는 것(schlafen)은 상태가 그대로라서 haben, 잠이 드는 것(einschlafen)은 상태 변화라서 sein이에요.<br>Ich <strong>habe</strong> gut <strong>geschlafen</strong>. · Ich <strong>bin</strong> sofort <strong>eingeschlafen</strong>.</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">haben · sein</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Ich ____ nach Busan geflogen.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) hat</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) habe</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) bin</button></div><div class=\"qe\">장소 이동 → sein, ich → bin.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Wir ____ den Film gesehen.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) haben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) seid</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) sind</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) hat</button></div><div class=\"qe\">4격 목적어 → haben.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Er ____ gestern zu Hause geblieben.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) bin</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) sind</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) hat</button></div><div class=\"qe\">bleiben → sein.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> ____ du gut geschlafen?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Hat</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Bist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Hast</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Ist</button></div><div class=\"qe\">schlafen → haben.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Das Kind ____ groß geworden.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) haben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) sind</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) hat</button></div><div class=\"qe\">werden(상태 변화) → sein.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Was ____ passiert?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) sind</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) habe</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) hat</button></div><div class=\"qe\">passieren → sein.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">7.</strong> Wann ____ du aufgestanden?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) hast</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) hat</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) bist</button></div><div class=\"qe\">aufstehen(상태 변화) → sein.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-F\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">F</span><h2>자주 쓰는 불규칙 과거분사</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">자주 쓰는 불규칙 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거분사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거분사</span>완료형과 수동태를 만들 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 대부분 ge-로 시작해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: gelernt · gegangen · verstanden</span></span></span>는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">원형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">원형</span>동사원형을 줄여 부르는 말이에요. 사전에 실린 동사의 기본 모양으로, 대부분 -en으로 끝나요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen · gehen · arbeiten</span></span></span>과 짝으로 외워요 — essen → gegessen · gehen → gegangen.</p></div></div><p>불규칙 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 원형·과거분사·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">보조 동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">보조 동사</span>완료형·미래형·수동태를 만들 때 두 번째 자리에서 인칭과 시제만 맡는 haben·sein·werden이에요. 화법조동사와는 다른 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe gelernt. → habe</span></span></span>를 한 세트로 외워요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>은 13과에서 덧붙여요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left\"><thead><tr><th>원형</th><th>과거분사</th><th>보조 동사</th><th>뜻</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>beginnen</td><td>begonnen</td><td>haben</td><td>시작하다</td></tr><tr><td>bleiben</td><td>geblieben</td><td>sein</td><td>머물다</td></tr><tr><td>essen</td><td>gegessen</td><td>haben</td><td>먹다</td></tr><tr><td>fahren</td><td>gefahren</td><td>sein / haben</td><td>타고 가다 / 운전하다</td></tr><tr><td>finden</td><td>gefunden</td><td>haben</td><td>찾다</td></tr><tr><td>fliegen</td><td>geflogen</td><td>sein</td><td>날아가다</td></tr><tr><td>geben</td><td>gegeben</td><td>haben</td><td>주다</td></tr><tr><td>gehen</td><td>gegangen</td><td>sein</td><td>가다</td></tr><tr><td>helfen</td><td>geholfen</td><td>haben</td><td>돕다</td></tr><tr><td>kommen</td><td>gekommen</td><td>sein</td><td>오다</td></tr><tr><td>laufen</td><td>gelaufen</td><td>sein</td><td>달리다·걷다</td></tr><tr><td>lesen</td><td>gelesen</td><td>haben</td><td>읽다</td></tr><tr><td>liegen</td><td>gelegen</td><td>haben</td><td>놓여 있다</td></tr><tr><td>nehmen</td><td>genommen</td><td>haben</td><td>잡다·타다</td></tr><tr><td>schlafen</td><td>geschlafen</td><td>haben</td><td>자다</td></tr><tr><td>schreiben</td><td>geschrieben</td><td>haben</td><td>쓰다</td></tr><tr><td>schwimmen</td><td>geschwommen</td><td>sein</td><td>헤엄치다</td></tr><tr><td>sehen</td><td>gesehen</td><td>haben</td><td>보다</td></tr><tr><td>sein</td><td>gewesen</td><td>sein</td><td>~⁠이다·있다</td></tr><tr><td>sitzen</td><td>gesessen</td><td>haben</td><td>앉아 있다</td></tr><tr><td>sprechen</td><td>gesprochen</td><td>haben</td><td>말하다</td></tr><tr><td>stehen</td><td>gestanden</td><td>haben</td><td>서 있다</td></tr><tr><td>sterben</td><td>gestorben</td><td>sein</td><td>죽다</td></tr><tr><td>treffen</td><td>getroffen</td><td>haben</td><td>만나다</td></tr><tr><td>trinken</td><td>getrunken</td><td>haben</td><td>마시다</td></tr><tr><td>tun</td><td>getan</td><td>haben</td><td>하다</td></tr><tr><td>werden</td><td>geworden</td><td>sein</td><td>되다</td></tr><tr><td>ziehen</td><td>gezogen</td><td>sein / haben</td><td>이사하다 / 끌다</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">sitzen · stehen · liegen</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">독일 남부·오스트리아·스위스에서는 sitzen·stehen·liegen의 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재완료<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재완료</span>말할 때 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. haben/sein + 과거분사로 만들어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.</span></span></span>에 sein을 써요 — Ich <strong>bin</strong> gesessen. 표준어는 haben이에요.</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-G\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">G</span><h2>가장 많이 하는 실수</h2></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 1</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">과거분사를 끝에 두지 않아요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe gelernt Deutsch.<span class=\"tx-n\">영어 어순</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.<span class=\"tx-n\">독일어를 배웠어요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거분사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거분사</span>완료형과 수동태를 만들 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 대부분 ge-로 시작해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: gelernt · gegangen · verstanden</span></span></span>는 언제나 문장 맨 끝이에요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 2</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">이동 동사에 haben을 써요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe nach Berlin gefahren.<span class=\"tx-n\">haben</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin nach Berlin gefahren.<span class=\"tx-n\">베를린에 갔어요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">목적어<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">목적어</span>동사의 동작을 받는 말이에요. 독일어에서는 주로 4격이나 3격이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich sehe den Film. → den Film</span></span></span> 없이 장소를 옮기는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 sein이에요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 3</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">불규칙 동사에 -t를 붙여요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe Deutsch gesprecht.<span class=\"tx-n\">규칙 동사처럼</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe Deutsch gesprochen.<span class=\"tx-n\">독일어로 말했어요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">불규칙 과거분사는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">원형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">원형</span>동사원형을 줄여 부르는 말이에요. 사전에 실린 동사의 기본 모양으로, 대부분 -en으로 끝나요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen · gehen · arbeiten</span></span></span>과 함께 외워요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 4</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">비분리·-ieren 동사에 ge를 붙여요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe meine Oma gebesucht. · Er hat gestudiert.<span class=\"tx-n\">ge 추가</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe meine Oma besucht. · Er hat studiert.<span class=\"tx-n\">ge 없음</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">강세가 첫 음절에 없으면 ge를 붙이지 않아요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 5</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">분리동사의 ge를 앞에 붙여요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe geeinkauft.<span class=\"tx-n\">ge가 앞</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe eingekauft.<span class=\"tx-n\">장을 봤어요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">분리동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">분리동사</span>앞부분(접두어)이 문장 끝으로 떨어져 나가는 동사예요. 접두어에 강세가 있어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: aufstehen → Ich stehe um 7 Uhr auf.</span></span></span>는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">접두어<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">접두어</span>단어 앞에 붙어 뜻을 더하거나 바꾸는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: auf-stehen · ver-stehen</span></span></span>와 동사 사이에 ge가 들어가요.</div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">실수 피하기</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> '나는 그 책을 읽었어요.'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Ich habe das Buch gelesen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ich habe gelesen das Buch.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Ich bin das Buch gelesen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Ich habe das Buch gelest.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">haben + 과거분사 끝, lesen → gelesen.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> '우리는 어제 왔어요.'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Wir sind gestern gekommen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Wir haben gestern gekommen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Wir sind gestern gekommt.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Wir sind gekommen gestern.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">kommen → sein, gekommen.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> '그는 사진을 찍었어요.'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Er hat ein Foto gemachen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Er hat ein Foto gemacht.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Er ist ein Foto gemacht.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Er hat gemacht ein Foto.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">규칙 → gemacht, haben.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> '나는 엄마에게 전화했어요.'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Ich habe meine Mutter anrufen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ich habe meine Mutter geanrufen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Ich bin meine Mutter angerufen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Ich habe meine Mutter angerufen.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">분리 → an + ge + rufen.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> '그녀는 베를린에서 공부했어요.'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Sie ist in Berlin studiert.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Sie hat in Berlin studiert.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Sie hat in Berlin gestudiert.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Sie hat in Berlin studieren.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">-ieren → ge 없음.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-H\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">H</span><h2>참고</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">현재완료의 부정</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">nicht는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거분사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거분사</span>완료형과 수동태를 만들 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 대부분 ge-로 시작해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: gelernt · gegangen · verstanden</span></span></span> 바로 앞이에요 — Ich habe ihn <strong>nicht</strong> gesehen. · Ich habe <strong>keine</strong> Zeit gehabt.(9과)</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">종속절의 현재완료</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">weil·dass <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">종속절<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">종속절</span>주절에 딸린 문장이에요. 활용된 동사가 맨 끝에 오고, 쉼표로 주절과 나눠요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: …, weil ich krank bin.</span></span></span>에서는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">보조 동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">보조 동사</span>완료형·미래형·수동태를 만들 때 두 번째 자리에서 인칭과 시제만 맡는 haben·sein·werden이에요. 화법조동사와는 다른 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe gelernt. → habe</span></span></span>가 맨 끝으로 가요 — …, weil ich viel gearbeitet <strong>habe</strong>.(20과)</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">sein · haben · 화법조동사는 과거형이 더 자연스러워요</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">말할 때도 Ich war krank. · Ich hatte keine Zeit. · Ich konnte nicht kommen.처럼 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>을 더 자주 써요(13과).</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-I\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">I</span><h2>바로 쓰는 문장 · 일상 회화</h2></div><p>지난 일을 묻고 답하는 문장이에요.</p><div class=\"exl talk-l\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Was <strong>hast</strong> du am Wochenende <strong>gemacht</strong>?</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">바스 하스트 두 암 보헨엔데 게마흐트</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">주말에 뭐 했어?</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich <strong>bin</strong> nach Busan <strong>gefahren</strong>.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">이히 빈 나흐 부산 게파렌</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">부산에 다녀왔어.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\"><strong>Hast</strong> du gut <strong>geschlafen</strong>?</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">하스트 두 구트 게슐라펜</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">잘 잤어?</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich <strong>habe</strong> das <strong>vergessen</strong>.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">이히 하베 다스 페어게센</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">그걸 잊어버렸어요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Was <strong>ist passiert</strong>?</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">바스 이스트 파시어트</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">무슨 일이 있었어요?</span></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"summary\"><div class=\"summary-card\"><h2 class=\"sum-title\">이 과 정리</h2><div><div class=\"sum-li\">현재완료 = 보조 동사 haben/sein(두 번째) + 과거분사(끝), 말할 때의 기본 과거</div><div class=\"sum-li\">규칙 ge-…-t(어간 -t·-d는 -et), 불규칙 ge-…-en(모음 변화), 혼합 ge-…-t(모음 변화) — gebracht · gedacht · gewusst</div><div class=\"sum-li\">분리동사는 접두어 + ge + 어간 — eingekauft, 비분리·-ieren 동사는 ge 없음 — besucht · studiert</div><div class=\"sum-li\">sein과 쓰는 동사 — 장소 이동(gehen·fahren·kommen), 상태 변화(aufstehen·einschlafen·werden), sein·bleiben·passieren</div><div class=\"sum-li\">4격 목적어가 있으면 haben — Ich habe das Auto gefahren.</div><div class=\"sum-li\">불규칙 동사는 원형 · 과거분사 · 보조 동사를 한 세트로 외워요</div></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\" style=\"margin-top:20px\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">다음 ⏭ 13과</span><div>13과에서는 글과 이야기에서 쓰는 과거형을 배워요 — ich lernte · ich ging · ich war.<br>sein·haben·화법조동사는 말할 때도 과거형을 자주 써요.</div></div></section><section id=\"solutions\" class=\"solutions\"><h2 class=\"sol-title\">Lösungen — 정답 모아보기</h2><div class=\"sol-grid\"><div><b>10·11과 복습</b>1. Ich stehe um 7 Uhr auf. · 2. verstehe · 3. darfst · 4. muss</div><div><b>과거분사 만들기</b>1. gemacht · 2. gearbeitet · 3. getrunken · 4. geschrieben · 5. gebracht · 6. gegangen · 7. gewusst</div><div><b>ge-의 자리</b>1. angerufen · 2. besucht · 3. studiert · 4. eingeschlafen · 5. vergessen</div><div><b>haben · sein</b>1. bin · 2. haben · 3. ist · 4. Hast · 5. ist · 6. ist · 7. bist</div><div><b>실수 피하기</b>1. Ich habe das Buch gelesen. · 2. Wir sind gestern gekommen. · 3. Er hat ein Foto gemacht. · 4. Ich habe meine Mutter angerufen. · 5. Sie hat in Berlin studiert.</div></div></section>\n<div class=\"brand-foot\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"foot-logo\"><div class=\"foot-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div><div class=\"foot-tag\">Innovative Learning Beyond the Traditional</div></div>\n"